==Indonesian==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|id|ms|sungai}}, from {{inh|id|poz-mly-pro|*suŋay}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{id-pr}}

===Noun===
{{id-noun}}

# [[river]] {{gl|a large and often winding [[stream]] which drains a land mass}}
# [[river]] {{gl|any large flow of a [[liquid]] in a single body}}

====Usage notes====
* It is usually capitalised when preceding a proper noun (''Sungai'' {{m|id|Kapuas}}, ''Sungai'' {{m|id|Musi}}, etc.)
** However, this rule is optional for {{m|id|Bengawan Solo}} (but not ''Sungai Solo''), since the word {{cog|jv|bengawan}} already means "river", or otherwise leading into redundancy.
* Some place names contain ''Sungai'', but they do not refer to an actual river. Examples include {{m|id|Sungai Penuh}} in Jambi, or {{m|id|Sungai Kunjang}} and {{m|id|Sungai Pinang}} in Samarinda, East Kalimantan.

